   "updated_at": "2026-10-27T18:52:27Z",
   "body": "The editor kept the model-id box's cleared value in its draft: clearing it set `draft.typed = \"\"`, while the draft it opened from has no `typed` key. `providerDraftValue` saw those as different, so `providerDirty` stayed true and Cancel asked to discard. The filter box itself stores nothing; the model box beside it was the one keeping the empty value.\n\n[fix/2669-gui-after-the-codex-editor](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/2669-gui-after-the-codex-editor), commit f8ddfd8d3991e4b3cb220b6c04137bbe3ff22675. It treats an empty or whitespace-only typed value as absent; a model id still typed remains unsaved, kept by Save as Enter would and dropped by Cancel.\n\nRun: the new test in `internal/gui/tests/provider-draft-picks.test.cjs` failed before the change (`nothing is left to discard: true !== false`) and passes after in Chromium and WebKit in all five languages (20/20 in that file; 40/40 across the related editor tests). `go build ./...`, `go vet ./internal/gui/` and `go test ./internal/gui/ -count=1` pass.\n\nThis is a fork branch, ready to review, not a claim on the issue's ownership.\n",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
